# Generated by tools/ from framework-metadata.json. The metadata-sync CI guard relies on these being
# byte-identical to a fresh regeneration; pin them to LF so core.autocrlf can't introduce CRLF on a
# Windows checkout and make the git-diff guard misfire. See docs/framework-metadata-ssot.md.
framework-metadata.json text eol=lf
claude-plugins/skills/**/references/*.generated.md text eol=lf

# Committed agent bundle (built by tools/build-agent-bundle.mjs, shipped in the npm package).
# Same reason as above: the CI/pre-commit bundle guard byte-compares a fresh regeneration, so
# pin LF to keep core.autocrlf from misfiring it on a Windows checkout. See docs/agent-guidance-distribution.md.
Angular/projects/spiderly/agent/** text eol=lf

# A nested CLAUDE.md (any below the root) and a rule file under .claude/rules/ hold at most 2,000
# bytes, as ci-workflows size-cap/size-cap.mjs reads these marks. Such a file holds only what bites a
# session before it reads any one symbol, so it never grows into a component manual. Claude Code loads
# every .md file under .claude/rules/, so the glob reaches subfolders too. Root CLAUDE.md keeps the
# general cap, 20,000 bytes: its line after the nested one unsets the mark, since the later line wins.
CLAUDE.md size-cap=2000
/CLAUDE.md -size-cap
.claude/rules/**/*.md size-cap=2000
# A rule file over 2,000 bytes keeps a mark at its size, and the text pass that cuts it under 2,000
# removes the mark.
.claude/rules/library-scss.md size-cap=2166

# What a script or tool writes, which the Size cap skips (ci-workflows size-cap/size-cap.mjs, run by
# .githooks/pre-commit and CI). The generators' own sources, NetAndAngularFilesGenerator.cs among
# them, are written by hand and stay unmarked.
framework-metadata.json linguist-generated
*.generated.md linguist-generated
Angular/projects/spiderly/agent/** linguist-generated
tests/e2e-fixtures/backend/entities/ZooShapes.cs linguist-generated
package-lock.json linguist-generated
# Verify's snapshots, which the tests write.
*.verified.* linguist-generated
